From 9db82cb4355d9dbe8c2812d9f05c30e4d227ae4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davanum Srinivas <davanum@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 10:41:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test/integration/conversion: drain watch goroutines before
 stopping webhook
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After apiServerTearDown() cancels the server context, etcd watch goroutines
that are already mid-event (inside serialProcessEvents → transform →
prepareObjs → decodeObj) continue processing until the current event is
done before checking context cancellation.

If a watch goroutine is converting a CRD instance via the conversion webhook
when webhookTearDown() closes the webhook server, it gets "connection
refused". fatalOnDecodeError (set via KUBE_PANIC_WATCH_DECODE_ERROR in CI)
converts this decode error into a panic, failing the test.

PR #136909 correctly ordered apiServerTearDown() before webhookTearDown(),
but did not account for goroutines already mid-event at the time the context
is cancelled. Adding a 2-second drain window between the two tear-downs
gives any in-progress watch goroutines time to complete their webhook calls
while the server is still reachable, eliminating the race.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/136739

Signed-off-by: Davanum Srinivas <davanum@gmail.com>
---
 .../test/integration/conversion/conversion_test.go           | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/staging/src/k8s.io/apiextensions-apiserver/test/integration/conversion/conversion_test.go b/staging/src/k8s.io/apiextensions-apiserver/test/integration/conversion/conversion_test.go
index 317bb2ff97a..6760e357cf3 100644
--- a/staging/src/k8s.io/apiextensions-apiserver/test/integration/conversion/conversion_test.go
+++ b/staging/src/k8s.io/apiextensions-apiserver/test/integration/conversion/conversion_test.go
@@ -1599,6 +1599,11 @@ func TestWebhookConversion_WhitespaceCABundleEtcdBypass(t *testing.T) {
 		// Ensure conversion webhook remains available until the apiserver
 		// and its etcd watches are fully shut down.
 		apiServerTearDown()
+		// After the apiserver stops, etcd watch goroutines may still be
+		// processing queued events that call the conversion webhook. Give them
+		// time to complete before closing the webhook server; otherwise they
+		// hit connection-refused and panic via fatalOnDecodeError.
+		time.Sleep(2 * time.Second)
 		webhookTearDown()
 	})
 
-- 
